sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as User / Client App
    participant Express as Express Gateway
    participant Mongo as MongoDB
    participant FastAPI as FastAPI AI Service
    participant VectorDB as PostgreSQL (pgvector)
    participant LLM as External LLM Provider

    %% Step 1-2: Request & Authorization
    Client->>Express: POST /api/v1/conversations/:id/messages { query, documentIds }
    Note over Express: 1. Authenticate JWT token & extract userId
    Express->>Mongo: 2. Verify conversation ownership & document access (userId match)
    Mongo-->>Express: Ownership confirmed & documents verified

    %% Delegate to AI Service
    Express->>FastAPI: POST /internal/v1/rag/query (query, docIds, userId, history)
    Note over FastAPI: Verify X-Internal-Service-Key

    %% Step 3: Query Embedding
    Note over FastAPI: 3. Generate query embedding via configured provider
    FastAPI->>LLM: Embed query text
    LLM-->>FastAPI: Dense float vector (dim: 1536)

    %% Step 4: Vector Retrieval
    FastAPI->>VectorDB: 4. Cosine similarity query WHERE user_id=$1 AND document_id IN ($2)
    VectorDB-->>FastAPI: Top-K passages with page numbers & similarity scores

    %% Step 5: Optional Reranking
    opt Reranker Enabled
        Note over FastAPI: 5. Rerank passages with cross-encoder / relevance scorer
    end

    %% Step 6: Grounded Prompt Construction
    Note over FastAPI: 6. Construct prompt: wrap passages in XML delimiters,<br/>frame text as untrusted data, instruct strict grounding & citation

    %% Step 7: LLM Generation
    FastAPI->>LLM: 7. Generate completion (messages + grounded context)
    LLM-->>FastAPI: Streamed / completed response with citation tags

    %% Step 8: Citation Extraction
    Note over FastAPI: 8. Parse structured citations (documentId, pageNumber, excerpt)
    FastAPI-->>Express: Return { answer, citations, tokenUsage }

    %% Step 9: Message Persistence
    Express->>Mongo: 9. Persist User Message & Assistant Message with citations
    Mongo-->>Express: Saved confirmed
    Express-->>Client: HTTP 200 OK { messageId, answer, citations }

    %% Step 10: Edge Cases & Failure Handling
    opt Empty Retrieval / Unsupported Question / Provider Timeout
        Note over FastAPI: 10. Empty retrieval -> return polite "Insufficient info" fallback<br/>Provider error/timeout -> return graceful degradation code
    end

